       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood-pressure benefit.\n\nHere are some ways I can proceed:\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum labeled dose.\n2. **Enter 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if you intend it. I'd add a note that the dose is above the usual maximum and was confirmed by you.\n3. **Add or switch to a second agent**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, if 10 mg isn't enough. I can enter that order if you give me the drug and dose.\n\nPlease tell me which you'd like. If 20 mg was a typo, I can enter 10 mg right away."
      }
